    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection per the spec. The endpoint is OfficeFloor function-injection based, so the work touched the small function classes in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline.\n\n**New behaviour**\n- **`identityKey`** is now `SHA-256` hex (64 lower-case chars) over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, replacing the old plaintext `telephone|email|householdId` string.\n- **Duplicate detection (409)** is keyed solely on this identity key: `EnsureUniqueIdentity` rejects a create whose key equals that of an existing **non-deleted** owner. The email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in the pipeline, so a blocked email is a 400 first.\n- **Soft match** now triggers when the identity key *differs* but `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`).\n- Two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** are no longer a hard 409 \u2014 they get created and flagged as a soft match, because the telephone is part of the key.\n- The separate household-duplicate 409 (from the computed `householdId`) is gone; `householdId` itself is still computed and used for household size/membership capping.\n\n**Files changed**\n- `Soundex.java` (new) \u2014 standard American Soundex.\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.java` \u2014 SHA-256 key from telephone/email/soundex, with an `of(Owner)` and an `of(OwnerFieldsDto)` overload.\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` \u2014 409 on identity-key collision.\n- `AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 soft match on soundex+postcode with differing key.\n- `DuplicateOwnerException.java`, `AssignHousehold.java` (javadoc), and `openapi.yml` (identityKey description/example) updated for accuracy.\n\n**Tests:** `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (asserts `[0-9a-f]{64}`) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (409 on identical payload) both pass, and the full suite is green.",
